---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Identify equipment"
  description="Help identify missing DCUO equipment names using Census snapshots and in-game tooltip evidence."
>
  <section class="prose account item-identification">
    <h1>Identify equipment</h1>
    <p>
      Help connect unknown Census IDs to the right equipment. Verified names
      appear on every player's profile.
    </p>
    <p id="identification-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
      Loading missing items...
    </p>
    <section class="account-card" aria-labelledby="missing-items-title">
      <h2 id="missing-items-title">Missing item names</h2>
      <p>
        Distinct IDs from saved equipment and augments. Counts reflect saved
        characters, which may have changed equipment since their last sync.
      </p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Census ID</th>
              <th>Characters</th>
              <th>Pending evidence</th>
              <th>Last seen</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="unknown-items"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <button id="unknown-more" type="button" hidden>
        Load more items
      </button>
      <p id="unknown-empty" hidden>
        No unidentified items in the snapshots checked.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section
      id="overlay-access"
      class="account-card"
      hidden
      aria-labelledby="overlay-title"
    >
      <h2 id="overlay-title">Publish item details from DCUO Companion</h2>
      <p>
        Refresh your linked character's equipment, then create a companion
        token. In DCUO Companion, open Wiki items, paste the token, refresh the
        list, capture item details and review them before sending. Choose loaded
        catalog items to capture items beyond your equipment. Captured names,
        icons and supported details create or update the shared item catalog
        immediately. Only definitions actually loaded by the game are captured.
      </p>
      <p>
        The token expires after 30 days and allows item contributions from your
        linked character session. Creating another token replaces the previous
        one.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/companion-items/">Browse companion item contributions</a>
      </p>
      <button id="overlay-token-create" type="button">
        Create companion token
      </button>
      <button id="overlay-token-revoke" type="button">
        Revoke companion access
      </button>
      <div id="overlay-token-result" hidden>
        <label>
          Companion token (shown once)
          <input
            id="overlay-token"
            type="password"
            readonly
            autocomplete="off"
          />
        </label>
        <button id="overlay-token-copy" type="button">
          Copy token
        </button>
        <button id="overlay-token-hide" type="button">
          Clear displayed token
        </button>
      </div>
      <p id="overlay-token-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </section>
    <section class="account-card" aria-labelledby="item-submit-title">
      <h2 id="item-submit-title">Identify an item</h2>
      <p id="item-sign-in">
        <a href="/account/">Sign in with Discord and link your character</a> to
        publish item names.
      </p>
      <form id="item-evidence-form" hidden>
        <label>
          Unknown item from your character{" "}
          <select name="itemId" required></select>
        </label>
        <p id="item-snapshot-time"></p>
        <p>
          <a href="/account/#equipment-panel">Refresh your equipment</a> first
          if you changed gear. For an uncertain slot, change one item, wait for
          Census to update, and compare the before and after IDs.
        </p>
        <label>
          Exact item name{" "}
          <input name="name" required minlength="2" maxlength="160" />
        </label>
        <label>
          Tooltip screenshot{" "}
          <input
            name="image"
            type="file"
            accept="image/png,image/jpeg"
            required
          />
        </label>
        <label>
          Evidence and item details{" "}
          <textarea
            name="evidence"
            required
            minlength="30"
            maxlength="4000"
            rows="5"
            placeholder="Explain which slot or augment this is, when the tooltip was captured, and how you matched it to this ID. Include the item level, variant, stats, and a wiki/source link where available."
          ></textarea>
        </label>
        <p>
          Crop to the item tooltip. Screenshots are resized and stripped of
          metadata before upload. They are visible to you and moderators. Your
          saved Census snapshot is attached for review; a matching character
          name does not prove ownership.
        </p>
        <button>Submit item evidence</button>
      </form>
      <div id="item-submissions" hidden>
        <h3>Your item submissions</h3>
        <div id="item-submission-list"></div>
        <button id="item-submissions-more" type="button" hidden>
          More of your submissions
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      id="item-review"
      class="account-card"
      hidden
      aria-labelledby="item-review-title"
    >
      <h2 id="item-review-title">Review item evidence</h2>
      <p>
        Check the tooltip name, item variant, snapshot slot and timestamp.
        Screenshots alone cannot prove an ID. Use before/after observations or
        an explicit source ID when needed. Publish only verified details; leave
        the article blank if no substantive page exists.
      </p>
      <label>
        Review status{" "}
        <select id="item-review-status">
          <option value="pending">Pending evidence</option>
          <option value="approved">Published mappings</option>
          <option value="rejected">Rejected evidence</option>
          <option value="revoked">Revoked mappings</option>
        </select>
      </label>
      <div id="item-review-list"></div>
      <button id="item-reviews-more" type="button" hidden>
        More evidence
      </button>
    </section>
    <noscript>
      JavaScript is needed for item identification. Existing wiki articles
      remain readable.
    </noscript>
  </section>
  <script src="../scripts/item-identification.ts"></script>
</Layout>
